# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Render / Netlify _redirects file for ui.tekivex.com.
#
# Why this isn't a single `/*  /index.html  200` catch-all anymore:
# The unified production tree contains FOUR independent sub-sites:
#   1. /                         — landing React Router SPA       (this file)
#   2. /security/, /getting-started/, /components/<slug>/, /recipes/<slug>/,
#      /blueprints/<slug>/, /quick-reference/, /themes/, /bundlers/,
#      /rsc/, /ecosystem/, /license/  — Astro Starlight static pages
#   3. /playground/*             — demo SPA (hash-routed internally)
#   4. /book/*                   — packages/tkx-book static catalogue
#
# A wildcard `/*  /index.html  200` rule rewrote EVERY URL — including all
# Astro paths — to the landing React app's index.html. Result: hitting
# /security/ or /components/button/ showed a "Not Found" because the
# landing SPA had no matching route, even though the Astro-generated
# index.html files existed on disk in the deployed tree.
#
# Fix: explicitly scope the SPA fallback to ONLY the paths the landing
# React Router actually handles. All other paths fall through to
# Render's static-file resolution, which serves Astro's pre-rendered
# index.html correctly.
#
# If you add a new top-level landing route (e.g. /pricing), add it here.
# If you add a new Astro top-level path (e.g. /tutorials/), do NOT add
# anything here — static resolution will find it automatically.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Landing React Router SPA paths — rewrite to /index.html so the SPA boots
# and the in-app router resolves the actual page.
/about               /index.html   200
/about/*             /index.html   200
/contact             /index.html   200
/contact/*           /index.html   200
/privacy             /index.html   200
/privacy/*           /index.html   200
/terms               /index.html   200
/terms/*             /index.html   200
/blog                /index.html   200
/blog/*              /index.html   200
/docs                /index.html   200
/docs/*              /index.html   200
/examples            /index.html   200
/examples/*          /index.html   200

# Legacy hash-routed Astro URLs (pre-flat-URL migration) → flat permanent
# redirects. Kept for inbound links from blog posts / external sites.
/#/                                 /                                 301
/#/getting-started                  /getting-started/                 301
/#/bundlers                         /bundlers/                        301
/#/css-system                       /themes/                          301
/#/rsc                              /rsc/                             301
/#/security                         /security/                        301
/#/ecosystem                        /ecosystem/                       301
/#/license                          /license/                         301
/#/components/:component            /components/:component/           301
/#/templates/:template              /templates/:template/             301

# NOTE: NO trailing `/*  /index.html  200` wildcard.
# Astro paths (/security/, /getting-started/, /components/*, /recipes/*,
# /blueprints/*, /quick-reference/, /themes/, /bundlers/, /rsc/,
# /ecosystem/, /license/), the playground SPA (/playground/*), and the
# book catalogue (/book/*) all rely on static-file resolution. The
# wildcard would intercept and break them — which is exactly the
# production bug this file was changed to fix.
